$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Azido-4,6-dimethylaniline (2a) Typical
procedure: Substrate 1a (60.5 mg, 0.5 mmol) and CuBr (7.2 mg, 0.05 mmol)
were added to a 20 mL Schlenk tube under Ar, followed by addition of
TMSN3 (131.5 μL, 1.0 mmol), TBHP (182.5 μL, 5.5 M, 1 mmol), CH3CN (2.0
mL). The formed mixture was stirred at 30 οC under Ar (1 atm) for 2 h as
monitored by TLC. The solution was then diluted with ethyl acetate (15
mL), and evaporated under vacuum. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel to afford product 2a.
3-Azido-4'-methylbiphenyl-2-amine (2j) The reaction of
4'-methylbiphenyl-2-amine 1j (73.2 mg, 0.4 mmol), CuBr (5.6 mg, 0.04
mmol), TMSN3 (105.0 μL, 0.8 mmol), TBHP (146.0 μL, 5.5 M, 0.8 mmol), in
CH3CN (2.0 mL) under Ar (1 atm) at 30 οC for 5 h as monitored by TLC
afforded 46.9 mg (53%) of 2j, brown liquid. Petroleum ether : ethyl
acetate = 60:1, Rf = 0.6; IR: (KBr) νmax 3480, 3380, 2107, 1610, 1467,
1297, 821, 775, 732 cm-1; 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.35 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
2 H), 7.28 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H), 7.06 (dd, J = 8.0 Hz, 1.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.95
(dd, J = 8.0 Hz, 1.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.86 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.96 (br s, 2
H), 2.43 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.2, 135.7, 135.6,
129.5, 128.7, 128.4, 126.7, 125.1, 118.3, 117.1, 21.1; HRMS m/z (ESI)
calcd. for C13H13N4 (M + H)+ 225.1135, found 225.1136.
