$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Aryl Azide Synthesis. An
amount of 1.44 mmol of aryl halide was dissolved in 0.3 mL of
1,4-dioxane. The obtained solution was added, dropwise, to a
thermostatted mixture of 1.8 mmol of [bmim][N3] in [bmim][BF4] solution
(1.2 mL). The composition of the reaction mixture was examined time by
time by TLC. In some cases, the reaction was quenched at a suitable time
to avoid the formation of overwhelming byproduct. For the less reactive
substrates, the reaction was followed for at least 24 h. Then, the
reaction mixture was extracted several times with diethyl ether. After
solvent elimination, the residues were separated by flash chromatography
on neutral aluminum oxide.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, alternative preparation shown, ionic liquid used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ionic Liquids/[bmim][N3] Mixtures: Promising Media for the Synthesis of
Aryl Azides by SNAr
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM D'Anna, Francesca; Marullo, Salvatore; Noto, Renato
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(16), 6224-6228

