$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Azido-4,6-dimethylaniline (2a) Typical
procedure: Substrate 1a (60.5 mg, 0.5 mmol) and CuBr (7.2 mg, 0.05 mmol)
were added to a 20 mL Schlenk tube under Ar, followed by addition of
TMSN3 (131.5 μL, 1.0 mmol), TBHP (182.5 μL, 5.5 M, 1 mmol), CH3CN (2.0
mL). The formed mixture was stirred at 30 οC under Ar (1 atm) for 2 h as
monitored by TLC. The solution was then diluted with ethyl acetate (15
mL), and evaporated under vacuum. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel to afford product 2a. 2-Azidoaniline
(2c)2 and 2,6-diazidoaniline (3c) The reaction of aniline 1c (46.5 mg,
0.5 mmol), CuBr (7.2 mg, 0.05 mmol), TMSN3 (131.5 μL, 1.0 mmol), TBHP
(182.5 μL, 5.5 M, 1 mmol), in CH3CN (2.0 mL) under Ar (1 atm) at 30 οC
for 4 h as monitored by TLC afforded 31.0 mg (46%) of 2c and 23.6 mg
(27%) of 3c, brown solid. 2c: petroleum ether : ethyl acetate = 30:1, Rf
= 0.3; IR: (KBr) νmax 3734, 3669, 2117, 1618, 1447, 1388, 872 cm-1; 1H
NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.04 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 6.97 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1
H), 6.80 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 6.70 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 3.81 (br s, 2
H); 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 138.1, 125.6, 125.2, 119.1, 118.4, 115.9;
MS (EI) m/z (relative intensity) 134.1 (100) [M]+. 3c: petroleum ether :
ethyl acetate = 60:1, Rf = 0.3; IR: (KBr) νmax 3445, 3335, 2126, 1587,
1486, 1465, 1286, 764 cm-1; 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.86-6.78 (m, 3
H), 3.94 (br s, 2 H); 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 130.1, 126.0, 118.4,
114.5; HRMS m/z (ESI) calcd. for C6H6N7 (M + H)+ 176.0679, found
176.0681.
