$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Azido-4,6-dimethylaniline (2a) Typical
procedure: Substrate 1a (60.5 mg, 0.5 mmol) and CuBr (7.2 mg, 0.05 mmol)
were added to a 20 mL Schlenk tube under Ar, followed by addition of
TMSN3 (131.5 μL, 1.0 mmol), TBHP (182.5 μL, 5.5 M, 1 mmol), CH3CN (2.0
mL). The formed mixture was stirred at 30 οC under Ar (1 atm) for 2 h as
monitored by TLC. The solution was then diluted with ethyl acetate (15
mL), and evaporated under vacuum. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel to afford product 2a. Methyl
4-amino-3-azidobenzoate (2g) and methyl 4-amino-3,5-diazidobenzoate (3g)
The reaction of methyl 4-aminobenzoate 1g (75.5 mg, 0.5 mmol), CuBr (7.2
mg, 0.05 mmol), TMSN3 (131.5 μL, 1.0 mmol), TBHP (182.5 μL, 5.5 M, 1
mmol), in CH3CN (2.0 mL) under Ar (1 atm) at 50 οC for 36 h as monitored
by TLC afforded 40.0 mg (42%) of 2g, brown solid and 24.4 mg (21%) of 3g,
brown solid. 2g: petroleum ether : ethyl acetate = 10:1, Rf = 0.4; IR:
(KBr) νmax 3473, 3366, 2116, 1685, 1617, 1265, 764 cm-1; 1H NMR: (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.70 (s, 1 H), 7.65 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 6.64 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 1 H), 4.27 (br s, 2 H), 3.87 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
166.4, 142.5, 127.8, 124.5, 120.1, 119.8, 114.2, 51.8; HRMS m/z (ESI)
calcd. for C8H9N4O2 (M + H)+ 193.0720, found 193.0723. 3g: petroleum
ether : ethyl acetate = 10:1, Rf = 0.2; IR: (KBr) νmax 3487, 3385, 2112,
1606, 1587, 1437, 1267, 1010, 759 cm-1; 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.53
(s, 2 H), 4.38 (br s, 2 H), 3.90 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
165.8, 134.2, 125.1, 119.6, 116.1, 52.1; HRMS m/z (ESI) calcd. for
C8H7N7NaO2 (M + Na)+ 256.0553, found 256.0559.
